---
description: Preserve Git history when renaming files/classes
alwaysApply: true
---

# Rename guidance

- If you’re asked to rename a file, directory, or any entity that maps to a file path, prefer a Git rename (`git mv` or equivalent) over delete+add.
- Preserve history even when changing the file contents: rename first, then modify the moved file(s).
- Avoid workflows that break rename detection (e.g., removing the old file and creating a new one with the same content).
- After a file rename, ensure the code still matches project conventions (for example, C# class/file name alignment) without reverting the Git rename.
